{"kind":"report","text":"SD-1 audit (request 2c343281, promise a2e29dc8), read from main 60223c5c.\n\nWhat the code assumes now: the row's presentation is a record of review, not a statement of the current presentation, and the matcher does not read it.\n- packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts:15-16 defines the field: \"names the presentation that the operator reviewed when they added the row; an older screen's client still compares it with its own.\"\n- applicationScreenHostMatches (:36) and bindApplicationScreenHost (:88) compare only directory and item.\n- The room serves only the item's current presentation (packages/scope/src/applications/route.ts:79-80 reads the installation for every screen request).\n- The sandbox (apps/sandbox/worker.ts:53-54) requires both Workers' rows to be byte-equal, presentation included. A move therefore needs both config files changed in one deployment, which the bidirectional deploy-smoke case already enforces.\n- Two readers still use the value. readApplicationScreenHost (:27) requires the key in a strict v:1 key set. Clients signed before U3 (1ec397ae) also require host.presentation === context.ids.presentation. Main 830d134a (Lending 0.5.0) and 66c70688 (Counter 0.6.0) are not descendants of U3. c8189f7c (Grow, demo) and 60223c5c (Lending 0.6.0) are.\n- docs/security/settings.md:99-100 states the rows as \"item 5 (Lending 0.4.0), presentation 188f7b84\" and \"item 2 (Counter 0.6.0) …\". That text, not the code, is what U4-B made false.\n\nDurable Object requests per screen load. These are counted from the code and the 0.6.0 asset list, not measured:\n- Today, each screen-path request (the 302 for \"\", index.html, each script, style, font and image, and _/context) makes 2 DO calls: Directory applicationRoom, then Rules applicationInstallation. A 304 revalidation pays them too, because the reads precede the ETag check. The /_application-host metadata request makes 0 DO calls: the sandbox calls screenHost over RPC, and the room reads its env.\n- Lending 0.6.0 has 19 assets. A first load fetches roughly the entry, the two scripts and styles, fonts.css, the fonts in use, the favicon and the wordmark, plus \"\" and _/context: about 10 to 13 screen requests, so about 20 to 26 DO calls before any native read.\n\n(a) Drop the presentation; the descriptor and matcher read the item's current presentation from the room.\n- Removing the key breaks every deployed client, including main's own: the strict key set rejects the descriptor and the screen fails closed. That includes Lending 0.6.0 and Counter 0.7.0.\n- The workable form keeps the key and has the metadata response fill it from the room. Then the field is true at every moment, and old and new clients both accept it.\n- Cost: +2 DO calls per load, about +8 to 10% of screen DO traffic. It also needs a head in the sandbox and the room service, plus a protocol note: the sandbox's both-ends byte compare must then exclude the field. The rows in config would lose the field, or keep it unused.\n\n(b) Keep it as a pin that a head moves.\n- 0 DO cost. The row can never equal \"current\" at all times, because an upgrade is a room act and a row move is a deployment. Between the two the row is stale one way or the other.\n- With the U3 matcher this staleness affects only one case: an item upgraded into a release signed before U3. All releases signed from now on are post-U3.\n- Every new release already needs a trust head, which already reviews its screen (U3 / d0a92549). That head can move the rows of the items scheduled to take that release, so (b) costs no extra head.\n\n(c) Leave it as it is: 0 DO cost and no head. The docs text stays false after each upgrade.\n\nRecommendation: (b), with the field named for what it is.\n1. Fix the false statement in docs/security/settings.md now: \"reviewed presentation\" plus the release it reviewed, and one sentence that the room serves the item's current presentation.\n2. Move a row's presentation in the trust head of the release the item will upgrade to. Each U4-B row needs one move at the next such head: 905a3f7e→70c32e9e and 188f7b84→6153d948.\n3. Optionally, a deploy-smoke check that each row's presentation belongs to a release in APPLICATION_TRUST.\nI do not recommend (a): it spends DO requests on every screen load to keep a field correct that only clients before U3 read.\n\nIf you choose (b), I can file the docs and row head now. It is config, docs and test only, so it needs the full gate."}